@startuml
title WebAuthn Passkey Flows with Custom Extension Server

actor User
participant "Browser (Client)" as Browser
participant "Authenticator" as Auth
participant "RP Server (WebAuthn)" as RP
participant "Custom Extension Server" as ExtServer

group Passkey Registration
User -> Browser: Triggers registration
Browser -> RP: POST /register/begin { username }
RP --> Browser: publicKeyCredentialCreationOptions containing extensions
note over RP
Returns publicKeyCredentialCreationOptions containing extensions
{
  "publicKey": {
    ...,
    "extensions": {
      "customData": [
        { "name": "extensionFunc1" },
        { "name": "extensionFunc2" },
        { "name": "extensionFunc3", "metadata": { ... } }
      ]
    }
  },
  "challenge_token": <JWT>
}
end note

group Custom Extension Processing at Client Side
Browser -> Browser: Read `extensions` from RP response
Browser -> Browser: Act on `extensions` → build customExtensions
  alt "If metadata says to call Extension Server"
  Browser -> ExtServer: POST /extensions/{extension_path} { username, data }
  ExtServer -> ExtServer: Verification, data extraction and storage
  ExtServer --> Browser: { status }
  end
end

Browser -> Auth: navigator.credentials.create(options)
Auth -> Browser: Attestation (clientDataJSON, attestationObject)
note right of Browser
Receive attestation to submit to RP.
end note

Browser -> Browser: Merge getClientExtensionResults() + customExtensions → payload.extensions

Browser -> RP: POST /registration/complete { webauthn, extensions, challenge_token }
note right of RP
• Verify attestation
• Verify extensions (presence/shape/proofs)
• Bind credential to user
end note

group Custom Extension Registration Verification
RP -> RP: Check required extensions are present
  alt "If metadata says to call Extension Server"
  RP -> ExtServer: POST /extensions/{extension_path}/verify
  ExtServer -> ExtServer: Verification and data validation
  ExtServer --> RP: { status, valid }
  end
end

RP --> Browser: { status }
end

group Passkey Authentication
User -> Browser: Triggers authentication
Browser -> RP: POST /authenticate/begin { username }
RP --> Browser: publicKeyCredentialRequestOptions containing extensions
note over RP
Returns publicKeyCredentialRequestOptions containing extensions
{
  "publicKey": {
    ...,
    "extensions": {
      "customData": [
        { "name": "extensionFunc1" },
        { "name": "extensionFunc2" },
        { "name": "extensionFunc3", "metadata": { ... } }
      ]
    }
  },
  "challenge_token": <JWT>
}
end note

group Custom Extension Processing at Client Side
Browser -> Browser: Read `extensions` from RP response
Browser -> Browser: Act on `extensions` → build customExtensions
  alt "If metadata says to call Extension Server"
  Browser -> ExtServer: POST /extensions/{extension_path} { username, data }
  ExtServer -> ExtServer: Verification, data extraction and storage
  ExtServer --> Browser: { status }
  end
end

Browser -> Auth: navigator.credentials.get(options)
Auth -> Browser: Assertion (authenticatorData, clientDataJSON, signature)
note right of Browser
Receive assertion to submit to RP.
end note

Browser -> Browser: Merge getClientExtensionResults() + customExtensions → payload.extensions

Browser -> RP: POST /authentication/complete { webauthn, extensions, challenge_token }
note right of RP
• Verify assertion
• Verify extensions (presence/shape/proofs)
• Issue session
end note

group Custom Extension Authentication Verification
RP -> RP: Check required extensions are present
  alt "If metadata says to call Extension Server"
  RP -> ExtServer: POST /extensions/{extension_path}/verify
  ExtServer -> ExtServer: Verification and data validation
  ExtServer --> RP: { status, valid }
  end
end

RP --> Browser: { status }
end
@enduml
